   "title": "Controller panel (read me)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "One control panel drives several nodes, like spare parameters on a Houdini null with relative references.\n\nParameters (PCG) declares three values: ring_radius, pillars and pillar_height. They are bound (from the target node's right-click menu, PCG bind-parameter entry) to:\n  - Circle: Radius X / Y <- ring_radius, Divisions <- pillars\n  - Tube (the pillar): Height <- pillar_height\n  - Torus (the top ring): Radius <- ring_radius\n  - Transform (lifts the ring): Translate Y <- pillar_height\nA bound widget shows its reference in its label. Change a value on the panel and every bound widget follows; only the nodes that use it re-run.\n\nThe chain itself: Circle points -> Copy to Points with a Tube whose base sits at y = 0 (Match Size) -> merge with the lifted Torus.\n\nNote: bindings are evaluated by the ComfyUI front end. Run through the API, the workflow uses the values last written into the widgets."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
